{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey Security Deposit Law","requirement":"A landlord may not collect a security deposit exceeding 1.5 months' rent, may increase it by no more than 10% yearly, must pay interest to the tenant, and must return the deposit less deductions within 30 days after tenancy ends.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; annual increase max 10%","coverage_conditions":"All residential rentals in New Jersey, except seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days by a person with a permanent residence elsewhere.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Seasonal use or rental for a term of not more than 125 consecutive days for residential purposes by a person having a permanent place of residence elsewhere.","penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19 et seq.","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act security deposit return after domestic violence termination","requirement":"When a tenant terminates a lease under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available within 15 business days and notify the tenant in writing within 3 business days of when and where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease due to domestic violence under the Safe Housing Act; does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"If a tenant terminates the lease agreement prior to the expiration of the lease pursuant to the Safe Housing Act , (N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6), the tenant is entitled to the return of their security deposit. Within 15 business days after the lease  is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
